      "math_academy_id": "q-37026",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $h$ defined by the following table?\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $h(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $h(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a table, the range consists of all numbers that feature in the row corresponding to $h(x).$\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2}\\}.$",
